# DocPilot — one key, for the provider you chose in your DocPilot config:
# docs/.vitepress/config.mjs, .vitepress/config.mjs or docpilot.config.mjs
# (`.js` is read for each of the three). The CLI uses the first path that exists.
#
# Nothing here reaches the browser. The key is attached in Node: by the Vite dev
# proxy while you develop, and by your own reverse proxy in production. A key
# written into `themeConfig` instead is a key published, because themeConfig is
# compiled into the client bundle.
#
# With none of these set the site still builds. The panel switches itself off
# and the build log says which variable is missing and what to run.

# ── local, free, no key ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# provider: 'ollama' in that config file. Nothing to put here.
#   ollama pull bge-m3        # the embedder
#   ollama pull qwen3:8b      # the model that answers

# ── hosted: pick the one matching chat.provider ──────────────────────────────
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# GROQ_API_KEY=
# DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=
# TOGETHER_API_KEY=
# FIREWORKS_API_KEY=
# MISTRAL_API_KEY=
# NEBIUS_API_KEY=
# XAI_API_KEY=
# CEREBRAS_API_KEY=
# CUSTOM_API_KEY=

# ── the embedder is a separate decision ──────────────────────────────────────
# Anthropic, DeepSeek, Groq, xAI and Cerebras serve no embeddings endpoint at
# all. OpenRouter is NOT one of them — it serves /v1/embeddings and publishes a
# catalogue of embedding models, so an OpenRouter key covers both halves and a
# second provider is one you do not need.
#
# With a chat-only provider, `embed: 'auto'` — the default — does not stop the
# build: it borrows OpenRouter's free embedding pool, which costs nothing and
# names no model. The part worth reading before you accept it, and the part the
# build prints on every run: the WHOLE CORPUS IS POSTED TO OPENROUTER AT BUILD
# TIME, and the borrowed half needs OPENROUTER_API_KEY set beside your chat key.
# Questions still go to the chat provider you named. A corpus that may not leave
# your network wants an embedder named explicitly — a local Ollama, or any
# provider above that embeds — and then the key above covers chat only.
#
# Or say there is no embedder: `embed: false` retrieves by BM25 alone and needs no
# key, no second provider and no vectors in the index. It is a real configuration
# and an expensive one — on one measured corpus recall@8 fell from 0.97 to 0.41
# and 11 of 44 answerable questions were refused — and the lexical channel scores
# zero for a question asked in a language the corpus is not written in. See
# `embed: false` in the config reference.
#
# The model that EMBEDS THE INDEX and the model that embeds a reader's question
# must be the same. A query scored against a foreign vector space is not a worse
# answer, it is no answer: retrieval silently degrades to keyword matching and
# the refusal gate starts refusing questions your docs can answer.
